// [99] the attested cross-border signature domains () render BYTE-IDENTICALLY on BOTH rails from the
// canonical spec, AND their generated coordination is GATED BY the M-of-N quorum guard — with no
// self-attest bypass, and the PostgreSQL admission threshold matching the spec's declared quorum. (The
// Solidity guard is deployment-parameterized — M/N are constructor args of ThresholdQuorumAcceptance, so
// the rendered contract does NOT carry the threshold; its checks are byte-identity + isAccepted
// consumption. Only PostgreSQL renders the threshold inline, so that is where threshold<->spec is pinned.)
// This is the coverage home for scenario-bearing ATTESTED domains: the generic [81]/[83] loops assert the
// UN-attested self-attest lifecycle (attest_ / 'missing attestation'), which an attested spec deliberately
// does NOT render (the quorum acceptance guard replaces it, /). A committed scenario is the
// transitional, output-independent eligibility signal for this legacy backend-golden gate (
// architect decision); an attested domain without one remains source/spec-only for this slice.
//
// REPOINTED (ADR section 9, ): this governed identity is KEPT, not retired. The Solidity rail's
// committed-golden diffs moved to the package's sources-only witness; what remains here is the quorum/
// threshold authority core still owns, plus an assertion that the externalized Foundry harness is neither
// re-emitted nor re-committed. Retiring the identity would have erased core's only statement that the
// responsibility left, which is indistinguishable at the next head from core simply having stopped looking.
//
// COVERAGE RATCHET (PR  review P2, reconciled with // ownership): eligibility is counted
// BEFORE generated backend artifacts are inspected. Every eligible domain must carry BOTH rails, and
// covered == eligible, so deleting either or both rails always fails even after the corpus grows. The
// four-domain floor remains pinned. This scenario discriminator is transitional; 's future
// architect-approved manifest is the final release-corpus authority and is deliberately not pre-decided
// here.
//
